tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3324077Z -- v5.3.0 — defrost: duty is measured, the derate is physics
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3324202Z   ok   the inferred estimator reads a real defrost as a PERFECT interval
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3324307Z   ok   an over-1 ratio can no longer park the derate above 1.0
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3324410Z   ok   five defrosting minutes in thirty is a duty of 1/6
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3324486Z   ok   and the interval counts as observed
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3324644Z   ok   a quiet interval is duty zero AND observed — that is real evidence
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3324745Z   ok   an unreadable flag yields duty zero but NOT observed
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3324862Z   ok   a defrost spanning an interval boundary keeps its second half
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3324987Z   ok   a sample stamped before the last does not subtract from the on-time
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3325059Z   ok   zero duty is no derate at all
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3325146Z   ok   the derate is 1 - duty x the loss multiplier
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3325257Z   ok   more duty is always a deeper derate, never a shallower one
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3325371Z   ok   and it is bounded below, so a latched flag cannot zero the pump
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3325462Z   ok   a measured bucket derates from its counted duty
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3325673Z   ok   and a measurement is never averaged with an inference of the same thing
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3325759Z   ok   an untouched bucket still derates nothing
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3325945Z   ok   the summary says which estimator a bucket rests on, and how many defrosts were actually witnessed
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3326057Z   ok   a duty outside [0, 1] is refused, not folded into the bucket
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3326209Z   ok   the range guard rejects only OUTSIDE [0, 1] — 0 and 1 still fold
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3326327Z   ok   a pre-v5.3.0 store loads without raising, and says it was upgraded
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3326413Z   ok   its learned factors are KEPT, not discarded
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3326523Z   ok   but the estimator's optimistic tail is clamped away on load
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3326631Z   ok   a measured duty then overrides the carried-over inference
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3326708Z   ok   a v2 store round-trips exactly
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3326825Z   ok   a v2 store still carries factors/counts, so a DOWNGRADE loads too
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3326934Z   ok   a garbage store loads as empty rather than raising (None)
