tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3394745Z -- #369/#370/#1738 — the duplication window can fire, and --record refuses a laundered regression
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3394886Z   ok   a copy in ANOTHER module is one copy, whatever its locals are called (#1738 a)
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3395001Z   ok   a third copy costs one more, not two more: copies, not pairs
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3395135Z   ok   a re-wrap or a comment moves nothing: the window is the AST, not the lines
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3395252Z   ok   the node floor holds: two short shared statements are not a copy
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3395368Z   ok   the shipped window is 2 statements of at least 30 nodes (#1738)
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3395585Z   ok   regression_rows names the metric that moved the wrong way, old and new (#370)
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3395735Z   ok   cross_seam_edges moving up IS a regression row: the retired ratio's band is gone
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3395879Z   ok   --record REFUSES a worsened metric by default and leaves the table untouched
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3396028Z   ok   an explicit --allow-regression reason lets it through and writes the new value
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3396167Z   ok   a blank reason is refused, so the flag cannot decay into pasted boilerplate
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3396316Z   ok   a pure tightening still records with no flag -- that is the point of the exercise
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3396445Z   ok   and the path that proceeds still stamps a resolvable recorded_at (#363)
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3396575Z   ok   cross_seam_edges is recorded like every other row -- a tightening lands
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3396704Z   ok   --allow-regression is a flag that demands a reason, not a bare switch
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.3396709Z 
