tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4050064Z -- Committed-fixture staleness (#347)
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4050168Z   ok   a key the committed fixture lacks is structural staleness
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4050282Z   ok   and so is a key the fixture has that the code no longer produces
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4050363Z   ok   and so is a leaf whose JSON type changed
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4050466Z   ok   a float that moved with the solver basin is not staleness
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4050545Z   ok   nor is an integer that flipped with it
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4050622Z   ok   nor is a boolean schedule that flipped
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4050712Z   ok   nor is a plan-derived list whose LENGTH moved
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4050810Z   ok   nor is a schedule this basin never populated at all
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4050917Z   ok   a payload with a float anywhere is not exact-comparable
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4051040Z   ok   the config-flow fixture is float-free, so the exact level covers it
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4051154Z   ok   and a solver fixture is not, so the exact level leaves it alone
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4051270Z   ok   a real fixture with every float, int and bool moved is not stale
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4051381Z   ok   and every one of those moves is still counted for the nightly
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4051475Z   ok   while the same payload with one key added IS stale
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4051602Z   ok   the exact level catches a string-valued move the structure cannot see
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4051703Z   ok   the gate fails on the float-free fixture's string move
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4051777Z   ok   and on the fixture that grew a key
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4051885Z   ok   and on a captured scenario with no committed fixture at all
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4052186Z   ok   but NOT on the solver fixture whose floats merely moved
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4052296Z   ok   which is still reported, because a nightly can act on it
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4052393Z   ok   and the gate's verdict counts only what it fails on
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4052474Z   ok   and the verdict NAMES every stale fixture
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4052576Z   ok   and says how many, how to re-record, and which need care
tests / fast (3.14)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-27T13:35:22.4052581Z 
